WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.416 --> 00:00:18.320
The man sitting in front of the fire was once more a younger version of Scrooge.

2
00:00:19.241 --> 00:00:22.522
However, the man had aged since the party at Fezziwig's.

3
00:00:23.922 --> 00:00:26.563
His face no longer looked shy and eager.

4
00:00:28.303 --> 00:00:31.404
Now there was a hardness in his eyes and around his mouth.

5
00:00:34.292 --> 00:00:36.933
The young woman beside him had tears in her eyes.

6
00:00:38.853 --> 00:00:42.914
Scrooge felt his heart twist with pain as he looked at lovely Belle.

7
00:00:43.875 --> 00:00:46.015
He had been in love with her long ago.

8
00:00:46.035 --> 00:00:51.877
"A new idol has displaced me in your heart," Belle said.

9
00:00:51.897 --> 00:00:57.858
"I hope it can cheer and comfort you in the future, as I would have tried to do."

10
00:00:59.899 --> 00:01:01.419
Ebenezer looked confused.

11
00:01:01.439 --> 00:01:03.840
"I don't understand.

12
00:01:05.072 --> 00:01:06.993
What idol has displaced you?"

13
00:01:07.013 --> 00:01:11.574
"Money," Belle said sadly.

14
00:01:14.275 --> 00:01:15.435
Ebenezer scoffed.

15
00:01:15.455 --> 00:01:18.796
"That's the way of the world, Belle.

16
00:01:19.896 --> 00:01:25.538
Soft-hearted people might say it's wrong to think about money, but nobody wants to be poor, do they?"

17
00:01:25.558 --> 00:01:33.540
"No, but it's possible to fear poverty too much," she said.

18
00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:37.741
"You've set aside all your other hopes and dreams.

19
00:01:39.242 --> 00:01:43.424
Now your only passion is making money, more and more money."

20
00:01:45.445 --> 00:01:46.405
Ebenezer shrugged.

21
00:01:47.205 --> 00:01:50.667
"That's because I'm wiser than most people in this world.

22
00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:54.809
And you're wrong to say that money is my only passion.

23
00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:00.151
My love for you hasn't changed at all."

24
00:02:01.812 --> 00:02:02.652
She shook her head.

25
00:02:03.724 --> 00:02:06.706
"When we first met, we were both poor but content.

26
00:02:07.946 --> 00:02:13.610
But you have changed, Ebenezer, which means your feelings toward me have changed too.

27
00:02:15.551 --> 00:02:18.672
Back when we met, you were a completely different man."

28
00:02:18.692 --> 00:02:24.035
"I was a boy," he said impatiently.

29
00:02:24.055 --> 00:02:26.857
"I didn't understand wealth back then."

30
00:02:26.877 --> 00:02:31.780
"It's something much more than that," Belle said.

31
00:02:32.864 --> 00:02:35.325
"That's why I've reached another sad conclusion."

32
00:02:35.345 --> 00:02:37.505
"What is it?"

33
00:02:37.965 --> 00:02:38.826
Ebenezer said.

34
00:02:40.486 --> 00:02:42.487
A tear slipped down Belle's cheek.

35
00:02:43.447 --> 00:02:46.988
"You once promised to marry me and take care of me.

36
00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:51.069
But I must release you from your promise."

37
00:02:51.089 --> 00:02:56.170
"What?" Ebenezer looked startled.

38
00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:59.971
"I don't want you to release me from my promise.

39
00:03:00.852 --> 00:03:02.112
So why are you doing this?"

40
00:03:05.313 --> 00:03:06.073
Belle sighed.

41
00:03:06.093 --> 00:03:09.775
"Because you aren't the same man who made that promise.

42
00:03:10.816 --> 00:03:13.337
Imagine if we were to meet for the first time today.

43
00:03:14.278 --> 00:03:16.739
Would you bother trying to win my heart?"

44
00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.001
Ebenezer hesitated.

45
00:03:20.021 --> 00:03:22.522
"Of course I would!

46
00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:24.583
You think I wouldn't?"

47
00:03:24.603 --> 00:03:29.226
"I wish I believed you would still try to win my heart.

48
00:03:30.286 --> 00:03:33.088
But I believe you would never choose a poor girl today.

49
00:03:33.972 --> 00:03:37.815
You'd never choose a girl with no family money to bring to a marriage.

50
00:03:39.216 --> 00:03:42.439
Not when you value everything in the world by how much it costs."

51
00:03:42.459 --> 00:03:50.385
"Belle, I Belle took a deep breath.

52
00:03:50.405 --> 00:03:56.110
"Therefore, with a full heart, I release you.

53
00:03:57.631 --> 00:03:59.953
May you be happy in the life you have chosen."

54
00:04:01.775 --> 00:04:04.957
Ebenezer opened his mouth again and looked ready to protest.

55
00:04:06.238 --> 00:04:10.600
But at the sight of Belle's determined face, he merely nodded and left.

56
00:04:14.863 --> 00:04:17.184
Scrooge watched Belle collapse in tears.

57
00:04:19.205 --> 00:04:20.826
"Spirit, show me no more!"

58
00:04:21.206 --> 00:04:21.707
he cried.

59
00:04:21.727 --> 00:04:24.428
"Why do you delight in torturing me?

60
00:04:25.449 --> 00:04:26.750
Please take me home!"

61
00:04:28.451 --> 00:04:30.252
The ghost stretched out its finger.

62
00:04:31.936 --> 00:04:40.278
"We must see one more Scrooge found himself in a different room.

63
00:04:41.459 --> 00:04:46.180
A beautiful young woman sat near the fire, and for a moment, he thought she was Belle.

64
00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.721
Then he spied a middle-aged woman nearby.

65
00:04:51.181 --> 00:04:55.022
That was Belle, and he guessed that the younger woman was her daughter.

66
00:04:56.503 --> 00:05:01.024
The room was in an uproar, with several children racing around shouting and laughing.

67
00:05:02.396 --> 00:05:07.541
Scrooge was so agitated by seeing Belle again that he didn't bother trying to count her children.

68
00:05:08.762 --> 00:05:14.747
Instead he watched as Belle and her oldest daughter laughed at the younger ones' noisy antics.

69
00:05:16.589 --> 00:05:22.954
Suddenly the door flew open, and a smiling man entered, his arms loaded with holiday gifts.

70
00:05:24.235 --> 00:05:29.380
The children raced over, nearly smothering him with hugs while shouting joyful greetings.

71
00:05:31.568 --> 00:05:34.870
The man finally managed to make his way past them to Belle.

72
00:05:36.731 --> 00:05:39.072
Leaning down, he gave her a fond kiss.

73
00:05:41.053 --> 00:05:44.555
Scrooge couldn't help imagining himself in the other man's place.

74
00:05:44.575 --> 00:05:50.718
"What if I had married Belle, as we'd planned long ago?"

75
00:05:51.199 --> 00:05:51.659
he thought.

76
00:05:51.679 --> 00:05:57.342
"What if I were the one coming home to a house full of children who were happy to

77
00:05:57.422 --> 00:05:57.902
see me?"

78
00:05:59.583 --> 00:06:00.804
Scrooge closed his eyes.

79
00:06:02.664 --> 00:06:06.787
"Stop!" he cried, trying to banish such thoughts from his mind.

80
00:06:08.228 --> 00:06:11.831
"Spirit, I don't want to see any more of this scene!"

81
00:06:13.992 --> 00:06:16.694
But the ghost sounded unmoved by Scrooge's pain.

82
00:06:16.714 --> 00:06:20.137
"You must see more.

83
00:06:21.658 --> 00:06:24.180
And you will see it."
